※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4557

※ A type parameter is one type in one call, so two places that say different
※ things about it are two that cannot both be right.  Nothing is widened to
※ make them meet, here as everywhere else.
※
※ Two *arguments* cannot disagree, the first settling the parameter and the
※ second then being lowered into what it settled -- which reports the ordinary
※ mismatch.  Two places inside one argument's type can, which is what this is.

fn both(p: 〈T', T'〉) → T':
    p⟦0⟧

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = both(〈1u8, 2u16〉)
    if n = 1u8:
        0u6
    else:
        1u6
